    "created_at": "2017-09-14T16:27:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-14T16:27:47Z",
    "body": "I'm guessing it would be acceptable if CSS had some kind of \"host element hook\" that HTML would use? That way CSS doesn't have to acknowledge the `legend` element explicitly. Having said that, CSS already acknowledges the `body` element explicitly (for `background` and `overflow`) so maybe this is not a big deal to just put in CSS?",
