    "created_at": "2017-09-14T23:13:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-14T23:13:50Z",
    "body": "Oh, and the order of this kind of style fixups needs to be considered as well. e.g. I would think this needs to happen before inlinification, otherwise it would creates a block inside places we only expect inlines.\r\n\r\nI guess probably CSS can define a concept e.g. inner-blockification which converts any \"inline-*\" to \"inline-block\" and other display values which generate boxes to \"block\".",
